SM-T715 tablet: the edge swipe does what the Back key does.

Past the on-screen keyboard and the shell's own surfaces (upstream's
BackLink, unchanged), Back asks t715-keys, the Back key's handler, with
SIGHUP: it closes a sheet or the drawer, is the previous page in a browser
and Escape elsewhere. When t715-keys is not running, upstream's Escape (by
wtype, or Hyprland's dispatcher by key code; Home for a terminal) runs, as
BackModel.BACK_ARGV's fallback. The SM-T715's 0.2.94 series' 0009, rebased:
upstream fixed the "key not found" of an Escape by name since, so the
fallback is kept. test/back-model.js gains the check; test/all and
test/back-surfaces.py follow. Against omarchy-mobile 8991845 (omamobile-shell
0.2.147), after 0001-0007.

